>
  <h2>Why train at home?</h2>
  <p>Home workouts remove common barriers like travel time, gym cost, and complicated equipment. A short, consistent routine can still build strength, burn calories, and improve energy.</p>

  <h2>Best home workout exercises</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Squats:</strong> legs, glutes, and core.</li>
    <li><strong>Push-ups:</strong> chest, shoulders, triceps, and core.</li>
    <li><strong>Glute bridges:</strong> posterior chain and hip strength.</li>
    <li><strong>Planks:</strong> core stability and posture support.</li>
    <li><strong>Mountain climbers:</strong> cardio, core, and coordination.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Simple full-body home routine</h2>
  <p>Do 2–4 rounds of this circuit:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Squats: 12–20 reps</li>
    <li>Push-ups: 5–15 reps</li>
    <li>Reverse lunges: 8–12 reps per leg</li>
    <li>Plank: 20–45 seconds</li>
    <li>Mountain climbers: 20–40 seconds</li>
    <li>Rest: 60–90 seconds</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Make it harder</h2>
  <p>Add reps, slow the tempo, shorten rest periods, or use dumbbells, resistance bands, or a backpack. Progress gradually so your joints and muscles adapt safely.</p>
